course: dictionary
lesson: 11661
title: Aspect: one side of a thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aspect is one part or side of a thing, a problem or an idea. When you think about one part of something, you are thinking about one aspect of it. The word is useful because it tells the reader that a thing has several sides, and one of them is being looked at.
explain: «We must think about every aspect of the plan before we start.» Here, every aspect means every single part of the plan: the cost, the time, the people and the risks. The clue is the word every, which tells you that many parts are being counted.
explain: Aspect can also mean the direction something faces, or the way it looks from a certain point. «The classroom has a south aspect, so it gets sunshine all afternoon.» Here aspect means the direction the room faces. Read the words around it, and ask: what does this word mean in this sentence?
fact: An aspect is one part or side of something.
fact: «Every aspect of the problem» means all the different parts of the problem.
fact: In geography, the aspect of a slope is the direction it faces, and this changes how much sunlight it gets.
fact: In grammar, aspect shows whether an action is finished, ongoing or repeated: «I am reading» is ongoing, but «I read» is a finished action.
fact: Common phrases: «one aspect of», «in all aspects», «the most important aspect».
exercise: «We looked at every aspect of the problem before we chose an answer.» What does aspect mean here? | The noise a problem makes | A map of the school | A type of cake | *One part or side of the problem
exercise: «The garden has a sunny aspect, facing south.» What does aspect mean in this sentence? | A kind of sunny weather | *The direction the garden faces | A very old tree | The name of the gardener
exercise: Find and copy the word that means one part of a thing. «Tom talked about one aspect of his holiday.» | holiday | *aspect | Tom | talked
test: «Mum looked at the problem from every aspect before deciding.» What does every aspect mean? | Every type of food | The colour of the problem | *Every single part or side of the problem
test: In grammar, «I am reading» and «I read» show different aspects of a verb. What does aspect mean in grammar? | *How a verb shows whether an action is finished, ongoing or repeated | A loud sound in a sentence | The part of speech that names things | How long a sentence is
exam: What does «a room with a south aspect» mean? | *A room that faces south | A room with a very old door | A room that is very dark | A room painted in gold
